From: OpenWrt Build System <openwrt@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] nss-dp: preserve QCOM ethtool MIB counter width

The paired SSDK fal_mib_counter_t exports u64 accumulated counters. QCOM
ethtool reads each field through u32, silently truncating the upper half
even though its netdev statistics path consumes the same u64 values.
Use the actual field width as already done for the XGMAC path in 011.

No counter offsets, names, quality flags, locking or packet path change.
This does not solve reset epochs, raw last-good or IRQ-off latency.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Base: NSS dataplane d8f802f08fd8ff31057ba58edb20bbe448e7b505 with local 011

--- a/hal/gmac_ops/qcom/qcom_if.c
+++ b/hal/gmac_ops/qcom/qcom_if.c
@@ -336,7 +336,7 @@ static int32_t qcom_get_eth_stats(struct nss_gmac_hal_dev *nghd, uint64_t *data, struc
 		p = (uint8_t *)mib_stats
 			+ qcom_gstrings_mib_stats[i_mib].stat_offset;
 		i = QCOM_STATS_LEN + i_mib;
-		data[i] = *(uint32_t *)p;
+		data[i] = *(uint64_t *)p;
 	}
 
 	return 0;
